Package: remotedesktop-server
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCHITECTURE@
Maintainer: Zeqian GAO <zeqian_gao@outlook.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/gaozeqian/RemoteDesktop
Depends: adduser, ca-certificates, debconf (>= 0.5) | debconf-2.0, libc6, libgcc-s1, libicu78 | libicu77 | libicu76 | libicu74 | libicu72, libssl3t64 | libssl3, libstdc++6, zlib1g
Description: Remote Desktop server (signaling, relay and ops console)
 Lets devices find each other and, when they cannot connect directly, forwards
 their traffic between them.
 .
 Three services are installed: the rendezvous server, which registers devices
 and hands out their codes; the relay, which carries the traffic of peers whose
 networks will not let them reach each other directly; and the ops console,
 which shows nodes, sessions, alerts and audit on 127.0.0.1:5090.
 .
 The installation asks which database to keep device codes in (SQLite, or an
 existing PostgreSQL server and its connection string) and whether signaling
 should use TLS: a self-signed certificate generated on this machine, an
 existing certificate, or plain HTTP. The same database provider is used by the
 console; with the memory-only choice the console still keeps its own SQLite
 file, because it cannot run without one.
 .
 The settings live in /etc/remotedesktop-server and are written by the server
 itself, so upgrading the package does not overwrite what the operator
 configured. The console keeps its data beside the signaling database and is
 loopback-only until a reverse proxy is put in front of it.
